      "tech": "Generative AI, large language model (LLM, including OpenAI, Claude, Gemini), RAG retrieval-augmented generation (Retrieval-Augmented Generation), vector database semantic retrieval (OpenSearch Service), AI Agent task agent (including semantic understanding, intent recognition, dynamic tool calling Tool-Use), document parsing and NLP natural language processing, Embedding model (text vectorization), evaluation algorithm (automatic scoring of resume and position compliance)",
      "benefit": "Solve pain points: Small and medium-sized enterprises generally face digital transformation dilemmas such as high AI technology thresholds, lack of professional and technical talents, time-consuming repetitive work, and scattered multi-platform services leading to high learning costs and accumulated subscription fees. Taking the human resources scenario as an example, it takes more than 5 hours for a single HR to process 100 resumes, and it still needs to take into account other tasks such as training, salary, and performance.\n\nBenefit description: This solution is expected to improve the efficiency of human resources-related tasks by 30% to 50%, the AI ​​response accuracy rate will reach more than 90%, and the system availability will reach more than 95%. Enterprises do not need to build their own IT infrastructure and can use it through a browser. The subscription system reduces the entry threshold. Specific functions include: automatic screening analysis and ranking of resumes, AI generation and automatic sending of interview invitations, and smart Q&A in the enterprise knowledge base (covering SOPs, regulations, and training resources).\n\nTechnical description: The system uses a three-layer microservice architecture and runs on the AWS cloud (ECS/EKS container service plus Lambda). The core is a cross-module AI task agent engine that operates in three layers: first understand the business needs of the user, then determine which system resources to use, and finally arrange the steps for execution. This set of Agents has the ability to call autonomous tools. Users can give instructions in spoken language, and the AI ​​will decide on its own which tools to call to do things, such as sending letters, checking calendars, and parsing files. It can be completed from start to finish without the need for human intervention step by step.\n\nThe platform also integrates large-scale language models from multiple major manufacturers, including Google Gemini, Anthropic Claude, OpenAI ChatGPT, etc. Users can switch between different models according to task needs in the same interface, without having to jump to different platforms to operate separately, nor do they need to pay for subscriptions. The system will automatically allocate the most appropriate model based on the type of task, such as using a model with strong reasoning capabilities for resume analysis and comparison, using a model with good quality to write invitation letters, and combining the strengths of each model.\nKnowledge retrieval uses RAG with a vector database to reduce the probability of AI giving random answers. The file parsing module can accept resumes in various formats (both PDF and Word). In terms of information security, VPC is used for network isolation and SSL encryption throughout the transmission process. Each customer's data is stored independently without interfering with each other.",
