      "benefit": "Solving pain points: During the machining process, a large number of unknown errors and risks are hidden, resulting in quality deviation over time and machine abnormalities. Finished product inspection alone cannot eliminate abnormalities, and heavy work and waste continue to occur. In mixed operations with multiple machines, multiple personnel, or cross-site and multi-supplier scenarios, it increases the difficulty of managing quality stability and cannot meet the requirements of the automotive, aviation, and military defense industries. Benefit description: Master the process quality of cooperating factories, create cross-factory quality visibility, standardize operations, and make quality transparent. Reduce abnormalities, reduce costs, stabilize production, and reduce inventory burdens. Technical explanation: Only when problems can be seen, standardized and digitized can the work site know which points need to be improved. Based on this concept, this program establishes a \"normal process standard model\" by extracting and analyzing machine vibration signal characteristics, such as: models of the normal status of workpiece installation centering, moving rails, grinding wheels/cutters, spindles and other machine parts that affect processing quality. It is used to determine whether the machine is in a stable and good product state, and to provide early warning of abnormal tendencies, identify possible abnormal items, and ensure that all types of processing production, such as stamping and grinding, are correct and consistent with the production conditions of the first good product, so as to achieve the goal of stable final production quality. In the AI ​​calculation process, data sets in different states are first analyzed, and PCA principal component analysis is used to extract representative features to form a dimensionally reduced feature data vector space. Then the GMM Gaussian mixture model plus proxy label technology (DBSCAN+KNN) is used to establish a classification and anomaly judgment model.",
